	"secrets.description.secrets": "<highlight>Secrets</highlight> securely store sensitive values such as passwords, API keys, certificates, and encryption keys. Stored values are encrypted and can only be decrypted using the <value>\"Show value\"</value> button. Values are stored by type: <muted>passphrase</muted> (password), <muted>certificate</muted> (PEM certificate), <muted>symmetric</muted> (symmetric key), and <muted>public/private</muted> (asymmetric key pair). Items marked 🔒 are system-managed secrets and cannot be deleted.",
	"secrets.description.containers": "<highlight>Containers</highlight> are logical groups that bundle multiple secrets. <muted>generic</muted> groups arbitrary secrets, <muted>rsa</muted> groups a public/private key pair, and <muted>certificate</muted> manages a TLS certificate, private key, and chain as a set. They are used for TLS termination on Octavia load balancers and for sharing certificates between services.",
	"secrets.description.orders": "<highlight>Key orders</highlight> asynchronously request encryption key generation from Barbican. Request a <muted>symmetric key (AES)</muted> or <muted>asymmetric key (RSA)</muted> with the specified bit length, and Barbican securely generates the key in the background and stores it as a secret. Generating keys on the server instead of entering them manually is safer because the keys do not travel over the network.",
	"secrets.description.quota": "<highlight>Quota</highlight> is the resource limit for this project. <value>∞</value> means unlimited. Contact an administrator to change the limits.",
